[{"id":5121816162,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMUi2Yg","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"a024a03e64e5cbd3c2748182132c5a2a7efe2207","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?u=081190c3a30acaf77c8531e0c6b9dae737767f58&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","login":"NoNormalDev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev"},"body":"Maybe it's good to also add a `ERR_FAIL_COND(!with_replace);` check to `_update_replace_preview()` for future-proofing? So if someone in the future adds another `_update_replace_preview()` call without the `with_replace` check it prints a single error instead of hundreds. It also suggests to the developer adding that call to check if `with_replace == true`.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123224#pullrequestreview-5121816162","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123224","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-09-05T15:19:45Z"},{"id":5122216281,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMU7RWQ","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"f3419374ce618403d96ac1dd0cebcf96fa62c9b1","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?u=081190c3a30acaf77c8531e0c6b9dae737767f58&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","login":"NoNormalDev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123224#pullrequestreview-5122216281","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123224","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-09-05T17:25:55Z"},{"id":5122357565,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMVD5PQ","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"1b1d4e702805ac124bdc50d581b02111b530ff0a","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?u=081190c3a30acaf77c8531e0c6b9dae737767f58&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","login":"NoNormalDev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev"},"body":"Fixes the issue. \n\nThe change makes sense, as `_update_replace_preview()` updates text in column `1` (second column) of a `TreeItem`, but if `with_replace` is `false`, it only has one column, not two, which causes the error. (also in a more general sense a function named `_update_replace_preview()` shouldn't be called if replacing is disabled)\n\nNeeds approval from a maintainer.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123224#pullrequestreview-5122357565","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123224","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-09-05T17:59:15Z"},{"id":5125909863,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMYctZw","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"1b1d4e702805ac124bdc50d581b02111b530ff0a","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?u=f0c85fe8c24debe91dc14d7efa97b51a19250b47&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","login":"kitbdev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev"},"body":"Tested, fixes the issue.\r\n`_update_replace_preview` is only called in one place, so either way its fine IMO. If it ever needs to be called somewhere else the error can be reassessed then.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123224#pullrequestreview-5125909863","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123224","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-09-06T16:15:50Z"}]